        acceptanceOrigin  "the rule of C16 for bubble temperatures, with its second term read as written (REVISED after the first run, and said so): the held-out bubble sets' largest stated expanded uncertainty (U95 = 0.15 K) plus the catalogue vapour-pressure model's error at the pure endpoints at the sets' pressure -- water's Antoine record puts its normal boiling point at 372.45 K against 373.15 K (measured against IAPWS, written in water.dat), 0.70 K -- so 0.85 K = 0.23 % of the held-out mean T (365.79 K). The first reading set that term to ZERO because no held-out set reports a pure endpoint; the vapour-pressure error is in every bubble point whether or not the endpoint is reported, so a perfect pair would have missed 0.042 %. For the binodal: 0.01 in mole fraction, as declared before the first run and NOT changed";
    }
}

);
